  "palette_method": "live PALRAM groups 4-7 at a frozen gameplay frame; A and B rotate which subpalette holds what.",
  "tile_sharing_scan": "NTARAM shares 156 cells by tile INDEX with skater A's set, but this is FALSE collateral: sprites use PT $0000 and background uses PT $1000 (PPUCTRL bits 3/4, register-confirmed), so the physical CHR bytes are disjoint within the 8KB bank. Zero FOREIGN OAM slots used skater tiles. Slot 0 is the inert Y=$BE tile-$FF junk sprite (no sprite-0-hit dependency evident; PPUSTATUS bit-6 polling not instrumented \u2014 flagged for Phase D).",
  "verdict": "CLEANLY SWAPPABLE (both skaters), same PT-disjointness basis as the surfer.",
  "coverage": "CAPTURED: idle pose for skater A and B, bank+palette+tile-sharing verified. NOT YET CAPTURED (TO-VERIFY, needs extended sustained capture): push/ollie-jump/trick poses and the full unique_tiles union across a 60s ride incl. later auto-scroll phases. The idle unique_tiles listed are the idle-pose set, NOT the complete motion set. Street Skate's short round timer + OAM clear-frame cadence made multi-pose capture expensive inline; recommend a dedicated pose-enumeration pass (freeze+step per pose) to complete before patching motion frames.",
  "capture_method_note": "OAM reads all-parked on clear/DMA-rebuild frames (peer-confirmed mechanism); captured via freeze-then-step + player-X spatial clustering + majority sampling. Grouping by geometry not slot, per NESdev flicker caveat."
